spans.s:
vāmaka,
(1) (Skt. adj., left), ˚kam, adv., on the left: devapuvrau pradakṣiṇaṃ vāmaku (= ˚kaṃ) supratisthitau (no v.l.) LV 〔219.17〕 (vs), stationed to the right and left;
(2) (unrecorded in this sense; = Skt. vāma plus -ka svārthe) charming: asaṃkhyeyaratna-˚ka-viracanālaṃkāram Gv 〔511.22〕 (prose);
(3) n. of a cakravartin king: Mvy 〔3571〕;
(4) (= Pali id.) n. of a great (brahmanical) ṛṣi: Māy 〔256.13〕.
